    "result_text": "All 70 tests across 60 suites pass with 0 failures. The implementation is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. The changes, driven by the V2 acceptance tests (Cp11/28/32/36/41/46/52/53/55/56/57/60):\n\n**Identity derivation \u2014 V2 tag mixed *inside* the identifiers**\n- New `OwnerIdentityVersion` centralizes the fixed `TAG = \"V2\"`, `API_VERSION = 2`, `SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`.\n- `OwnerRegion.identityRegion(...)` returns the plain region prefixed with `V2` (e.g. `V2NSW`) \u2014 the region code used *inside* the memberId. `AssignMemberId` now uses it, so every `memberId` becomes `V2NSW26\u2026` and can never equal a V1 value.\n- `OwnerIdentity.identityKey(...)` mixes `|V2` into the SHA-256 input (still lowercase 64-hex; duplicate detection stays self-consistent).\n- `AssignHouseholdId` mixes `|V2` into its hash while remaining a pure function of `(lastName, postcode)`, so households still share their id.\n\n**Response shape**\n- `openapi.yml`: added a top-level integer `apiVersion` and a nested `identity` object (new `OwnerIdentity` schema holding `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`); removed those three from the top level.\n- `OwnerMapper`: builds the nested `OwnerIdentityDto`, sets `apiVersion = 2`, and \u2014 critically \u2014 **decouples** `locality`/`timezone`/`ownerSegment`/`fiscalYear` from the memberId so they keep reading the *plain* region (`NSW`), never the `V2` tag. `deriveLocality` now uses `OwnerRegion.fromPostcodeOrCity` and `deriveFiscalYear` uses `FiscalYear.label` directly.\n\n**Audit**\n- `AuditOwnerCreatedEvent` moved to schema version 2: added `schemaVersion` (2), owner segment recomputed from the V2 identity (the memberId it emits is now the V2 value).\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. The V2 tag appears only inside the identifiers \u2014 confirmed by test output (`memberId=V2NSW26\u2026`, `\"schemaVersion\":2`) while `locality` stays `NSW`.",
